WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.100
Want to know whether anyone else has this problem?

2
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:12.600
It is out there, spread across a hundred threads.

3
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:20.600
Someone wanting to know what the chefs ordered last week.

4
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:26.600
That is your landing page, written by a customer.

5
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:34.600
Someone else keeping prices in six spreadsheets.

6
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:40.600
Two posts, both one click away. We say two because we read two.

7
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:48.600
Somebody has already built this. Still working on it last week.

8
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:55.400
Either you have a competitor you did not know about, or a head start you can use.

9
00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:03.400
Another was abandoned in 2024.

10
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:09.500
Find out why they stopped before you spend a year finding out yourself.

11
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.500
Where the idea does not turn up is next.
